course: dictionary
lesson: 14838
title: Pictures from inside
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a hard word from the words around it, which are its context. «The doctor studied a radiographic image of my knee to see if the bone was broken.» The words image and knee tell you it is a picture of the inside of the body, so radiographic must be about X-ray pictures.
explain: «The engineer ran a radiographic test on the metal pipe to look for hidden cracks.» Here the clues are metal pipe and cracks. Radiographic does not only mean people: it can also describe tests that look inside objects.
explain: Always check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The doctor studied an X-ray picture of my knee» still makes sense, so you have the right idea. When you are unsure, look the word up in a dictionary.
fact: Radiographic means to do with X-ray pictures and other images of the inside of the body or objects.
fact: A radiographic image is an X-ray picture, such as a picture of a knee.
fact: A radiographic test is made using X-rays, and engineers use these tests to find cracks in metal.
fact: Radiographers are the people who take radiographic pictures in hospitals.
fact: Other useful phrases are «radiographic examination» and «radiographic evidence».
exercise: «The doctor studied a radiographic image of my knee.» What is a radiographic image? | *A picture made with X-rays | A loud noise from the hospital | A kind of running shoe | A bandage for a sore knee
exercise: «The engineer ran a radiographic test on the metal pipe.» What was the test looking for? | The price of the pipe | *Cracks inside the metal | The name of the factory | The colour of the paint
exercise: Which word means a person who takes X-ray pictures in a hospital? | Chef | *Radiographer | Librarian | Surgeon
test: What does the phrase «radiographic evidence» most likely mean? | A story about a dragon | A list of shopping | Proof from a football match | *Proof shown by X-ray pictures
test: Which sentence uses radiographic correctly? | We ate a radiographic sandwich for lunch. | The radiographic class sang a song. | The radiographic cat jumped onto the table. | *The nurse showed us a radiographic picture of my broken arm.
exam: Which meaning fits radiographic best? | *Made with X-rays, or to do with pictures of the inside of the body or objects | Painted by hand in bright colours | Made with music, or to do with singing | To do with the weather and rain
